<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Trigonometric Functions — amplitude and period from a formula</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the function \( y = {@fx@} \), with \(x\) in radians.</p>
<ol class="tb-parts">
  <li><p>State the amplitude.</p>
    <div>[[input:ans_amp]] [[validation:ans_amp]] [[feedback:prt_amp]]</div></li>
  <li><p>State the period, in radians. Type \(\pi\) as <code>pi</code>.</p>
    <div>[[input:ans_period]] [[validation:ans_period]] [[feedback:prt_period]]</div></li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>For \(y = A\sin(Bx)\) or \(y = A\cos(Bx)\) with \(B > 0\):</p>
<ul>
  <li>the <strong>amplitude</strong> is \(|A|\), the height of a peak above the centre line. It is a distance, so it is never negative. A negative \(A\) only reflects the graph in the \(x\)-axis.</li>
  <li>the <strong>period</strong> is \(\dfrac{2\pi}{B}\). The basic curve repeats every \(2\pi\), and multiplying \(x\) by \(B\) squeezes it horizontally by a factor of \(B\), so it repeats \(B\) times as often.</li>
</ul>
<p>Here \(A = {@amp@}\) and \(B = {@b@}\), so the amplitude is \(|{@amp@}| = {@ta_amp@}\) and the period is \(\dfrac{2\pi}{ {@b@} } = {@ta_period@}\).</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of the function over two periods. Dashed horizontal lines mark the maximum and minimum heights, and a bracket marks one period along the x-axis.">
[[jsxgraph width="400px" height="240px"]]
(function() {
  var A = {#amp#}, B = {#b#}, T = 2*Math.PI/B, trig = {#trig#};
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-0.15*T, 1.5*Math.abs(A) + 0.5, 2.1*T, -1.5*Math.abs(A) - 0.5], axis: true, grid: false,
    showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false
  });
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x){ return trig === 0 ? A*Math.sin(B*x) : A*Math.cos(B*x); }, 0, 2*T], {strokeColor:'#003399', strokeWidth:2});
  b.create('line', [[0, Math.abs(A)], [1, Math.abs(A)]], {strokeColor:'#cc0000', dash:2, strokeWidth:1, fixed:true});
  b.create('line', [[0, -Math.abs(A)], [1, -Math.abs(A)]], {strokeColor:'#cc0000', dash:2, strokeWidth:1, fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [[0, -1.25*Math.abs(A)], [T, -1.25*Math.abs(A)]], {strokeColor:'#006600', strokeWidth:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [T/2, -1.25*Math.abs(A) - 0.35, 'one period'], {anchorX:'middle', fixed:true, color:'#006600'});
  b.create('text', [1.6*T, 1.25*Math.abs(A) + 0.2, 'amplitude ' + Math.abs(A)], {anchorX:'middle', fixed:true, color:'#cc0000'});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
